---
permalink: /admin/
title: "Overview | Admin"
bodyScripts:
  - src: "/scripts/admin-overview.js"
    type: "module"
  - src: "/scripts/contact-widget.js"
    type: "module"
  - src: "/scripts/palette.js"
    type: "module"
---
<section class="app-page">

  {% include "chrome/admin-sections.njk" %}

  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-text mb-2">Overview</h1>
  <p class="text-brand-muted mb-8">
    What is running, what has arrived, and what is waiting for you.
  </p>

  {# One live region, the same rule every Admin page follows. #}
  <div id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="mb-6 text-sm"></div>

  {# --- what is waiting for you ------------------------------------------
     Two numbers, each a link to the page that resolves it. A count you cannot act on is
     decoration; a count that takes you to the queue is the whole point of an overview. #}
  <ul class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 mb-10">
    <li>
      <a href="/admin/accounts/" class="stat-card group">
        <span class="stat-label">
          {% icon "fa-solid-users", "h-4 w-4 text-brand-muted" %}<span>Awaiting approval</span>
        </span>
        {# A stable slot, not an inserted badge. The number arrives about a second after the
           page does, and a figure that appears from nothing shifts everything under it. #}
        <span id="pendingCount" class="stat-number" data-loading="1">—</span>
        <span id="pendingNote" class="stat-note">Checking…</span>
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/admin/messages/" class="stat-card group">
        <span class="stat-label">
          {% icon "fa-solid-envelope-open-text", "h-4 w-4 text-brand-muted" %}<span>Unread messages</span>
        </span>
        <span id="unreadCount" class="stat-number" data-loading="1">—</span>
        <span id="unreadNote" class="stat-note">Checking…</span>
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  {# --- what is running ---------------------------------------------------
     Both of these are things this page can actually find out: the API answers /health with the
     time it started, and the app serves its own /build.txt. Nothing here is inferred. #}
  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-text mb-1">Services</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-brand-muted mb-4">
    Checked when this page loaded.
    <a href="/admin/health/" class="text-brand-accent underline hover:no-underline">Deploy history</a>
    is on the Health page.
  </p>

  <ul class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 mb-10">
    <li class="card">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-text">API</h3>
        <span id="apiState" class="status-pill status-pill--unknown">Checking…</span>
      </div>
      <p class="hint">api.tzortzoglou.eu</p>
      <p id="apiDetail" class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-muted">&nbsp;</p>
    </li>
    <li class="card">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-text">App</h3>
        <span id="appState" class="status-pill status-pill--unknown">Checking…</span>
      </div>
      <p class="hint">app.tzortzoglou.eu</p>
      <p id="appDetail" class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-muted">&nbsp;</p>
    </li>
  </ul>

  {# --- traffic -----------------------------------------------------------
     This card used to say the counter was "not connected yet", because GoatCounter's statistics
     needed an API token and a token cannot live in a page anyone can view the source of. That is
     no longer the situation: the counting is first-party now, the figures come from the API's own
     table, and /admin/analytics/ draws them. The card stayed a link and became a true one.

     Still no number on this page, and still deliberately. Every figure on Analytics belongs to a
     window the reader chose, and a single count lifted out of that context here would be a
     statistic with its meaning left behind - which is the same reason an invented sparkline was
     refused before. #}
  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-text mb-1">Traffic</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-brand-muted mb-4">Page views of both properties, counted by the API itself.</p>

  <a href="/admin/analytics/" class="card block hover:border-brand-accent/40 transition-colors duration-200">
    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-text">Analytics</h3>
        <p class="hint mt-1 max-w-prose">
          Views per day, the busiest pages of each property and where visitors arrived from, over
          a window you choose. No third party is involved. A row carries a visitor number that one
          browser keeps for a day, so the panel can say how many browsers a day's views came from;
          it carries no address and no account.
        </p>
      </div>
      {% icon "fa-solid-chart-line", "h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-brand-muted" %}
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold text-brand-accent">
      Open the dashboard →
    </p>
  </a>

</section>
